>set of NH3.0 sources with patches 1-4 *already* applied?  I can get
>the original source and the patch kits easily, but have trouble when
>I try to apply the patches.
>
>Thanks in advance.

I have had much the same trouble.  In my case, I tracked it down to extra
'return' characters that were added in various source files, presumably
in the transport process somewhere.  Many of them were pretty obvious,
because they were added in the middle of a word, and thus made the syntax
illegal.  Some were only found when patch had trouble.

This has been a major pain.  It seems only to affect the games sources
group, at least at this site.  I sure do wish these archivable moderated
groups were using 'brik' or some other portable and reliable checksum
scheme.  (Brik works with big checksums, and works identically on
machines with any byte order.  I get the same answers on my 68000 and *86
as are posted by vaxen.)  That way, we might have a reasonable way to
know right off when we need a new copy, and with timely information,
we might be able to find out where the sources are getting trashed, and
fix it.


